		{"id":"84d1b4adf6dedae9","type":"link","url":"https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/composite/index.html","x":12994,"y":6556,"width":886,"height":400},
		{"id":"d3542db637a041d8","type":"text","text":"## Scene building, Karma rendering, Image processing\n\n- [Solaris and Karma](https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/solaris/index.html \"Solaris is the umbrella name for Houdini’s scene building, look development, and Karma rendering tools based on the Universal Scene Description (USD) framework.\")\n    \n    Solaris is the umbrella name for Houdini’s scene building, look development, and Karma rendering tools based on the Universal Scene Description (USD) framework.\n    \n- [Copernicus](https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/copernicus/index.html \"Houdini’s 2D and 3D GPU image processing framework.\")\n    \n    Houdini’s 2D and 3D GPU image processing framework.\n    \n- [Compositing](https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/composite/index.html \"Houdini’s compositing networks let you create and manipulate images such as renders.\")\n    \n    Houdini’s compositing networks let you create and manipulate images such as renders.\n    \n\n## Mantra rendering and shading [¶](https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/#mantra-rendering-and-shading)\n\n- [Mantra rendering](https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/render/index.html \"How to render images and animation with the Mantra engine.\")\n    \n    How to render images and animation with the Mantra engine.\n    \n- [Mantra materials](https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/shade/index.html \"How to assign materials and create custom materials for shading.\")\n    \n    How to assign materials and create custom materials for shading.","x":14385,"y":6568,"width":1052,"height":377},
		{"id":"1b05204d5b1080ba","type":"file","file":"Images/Intro/HoudiniFirstSteps/5_Render.png","x":14198,"y":5316,"width":924,"height":520},
		{"id":"7854ed9dabc909ff","type":"text","text":"Text\n\nNow, we will quickly go through basic pipeline for modeling, export and rendering.\n\nFirst, we will create new Houdini project and file.\n\nThen, we will import existing 3D model from sites like Polyhaven.\n\nExample procedural operations will be performed on geometry.\n\nFor rendering, we will use Solaris desktop via `stage/` network. There we will link 3D model, add material, light, camera and karma renderer.\n\nFor exporting, we will use file node in `obj/geo/` network.\n\n\n\n","x":11686,"y":7200,"width":809,"height":374,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"9b46cb4c5308bd9b","type":"text","text":"UI:\n\n* Create project\n* Save file inside project\n* Check ENV variables in Edit -> Aliases and Variables...\n---\n* 3D viewport + manipulation (left side) + visualization (right side)\n* 3D viewport manipulation (left side)\n\t* 3D viewport camera icon\n\t* 3D viewport handle icon\n* 3D viewport visualization (right side)\n\t* Display options\n\t* Points\n\t* Normals\n* 3D viewport navigation:\n\t* LMB and drag\n\t* MMB and drag\n\t* Mouse wheel\n* Network pane\n* Network pane navigation:\n\t* MMB and drag\n\t* Mouse wheel\n* Parameter pane\n* Desktop presets\n* Shelves \n* Animation frame timeline\n---\n* Node selection \n* Node display\n* Node template\n* Node bypass\n* Node info\n* Node spreadsheet\n* Node selection vs Node display\n* Node cooking\n---\n*  ensure that network /obj/geo/ is selected\n\t* Scene view (3D viewport)\n\t* Network\n\t* Parameters","x":12634,"y":7200,"width":650,"height":1242},
		{"id":"820bdb0a9d102e6c","type":"text","text":"https://vimeo.com/737654649","x":-9772,"y":-1862,"width":297,"height":65},
		{"id":"2ad3233affac2c36","type":"file","file":"Images/Intro/ProcModelingApps/MotionGraphics2.jpg","x":-10011,"y":-1412,"width":607,"height":305},
