		{"id":"3dbd98bf466e242a","type":"text","text":"Computer science with focus on graphics and procedural modeling\n\n* https://kluedo.ub.rptu.de/frontdoor/index/index/docId/8211\n* https://www.itwm.fraunhofer.de/en/departments/bv/image-processing-ai-applications.html\n* https://vis.cs.rptu.de/","x":-15064,"y":-2001,"width":533,"height":200},
		{"id":"21f44e8d36489317","type":"file","file":"Images/Intro/AboutMe/FragmentDigital/FD_HCP_1.jpg","x":-14026,"y":-3940,"width":400,"height":217},
		{"id":"26b067769158d784","type":"file","file":"Images/Intro/AboutMe/RPTU/PHD_8.jpg","x":-14040,"y":-2225,"width":400,"height":303},
		{"id":"aba96f8a51d78b2e","type":"file","file":"Images/Intro/AboutMe/RPTU/PHD_22.jpg","x":-14040,"y":-1878,"width":399,"height":275},
		{"id":"bb0d6e9a42306b80","type":"text","text":"# Procedural modeling: Introduction","x":-17207,"y":-480,"width":850,"height":78},
		{"id":"aae4089798377d38","type":"text","text":"Dr.-Ing. Lovro Bosnar\nContact: lovro.bosnar@fer.hr","x":-17207,"y":-360,"width":360,"height":72},
		{"id":"5118cd367f9af239","type":"text","text":"About me.\n","x":-15366,"y":-379,"width":250,"height":82},
		{"id":"eabf6e3490a10c1d","type":"text","text":"Computer science. Main interests:\n* Graphics & procedural modeling \n* Growth, morphogenesis, fractals, chaos, etc.\n\nThesis: https://repozitorij.fer.unizg.hr/islandora/object/fer:5689","x":-15068,"y":-966,"width":537,"height":224},
		{"id":"4a61d8cd060a4fdc","type":"text","text":"University (FER)","x":-15366,"y":-884,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"7318efab0f114711","type":"file","file":"Images/Intro/AboutMe/FER/DLA.png","x":-14460,"y":-1260,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"bdc95067a0012569","type":"file","file":"Images/Intro/AboutMe/FER/M_2.jpg","x":-14029,"y":-1260,"width":469,"height":251},
		{"id":"1326e4ae2d0ecd4b","type":"text","text":"Links:\n* https://www.researchgate.net/figure/Simulation-of-the-2D-and-3D-Eden-growth-models-up-to-time-10-000-and-30-000-respectively_fig2_368332707\n* https://algorithmicbotany.org/papers/colonization.egwnp2007.large.pdf\n* https://paulbourke.net/fractals/dla/\n* https://natureofcode.com/fractals/\n* https://iquilezles.org/articles/juliasets3d/","x":-14451,"y":-540,"width":657,"height":243},
		{"id":"68ecbf63bc2c691e","type":"text","text":"PhD (RPTU)","x":-15366,"y":-1931,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"48a31836d0e9147f","type":"file","file":"Images/Intro/AboutMe/FragmentDigital/FD_PG_2.jpg","x":-14044,"y":-3437,"width":400,"height":212},
		{"id":"e8cccc3d8d1e89b3","type":"file","file":"Images/Intro/AboutMe/FragmentDigital/FD_S3D_4.jpg","x":-14460,"y":-2853,"width":400,"height":225},
		{"id":"0a8c71c0a2708e97","type":"file","file":"Images/Intro/AboutMe/FragmentDigital/FD_MC_3.jpg","x":-14460,"y":-3178,"width":400,"height":294},
		{"id":"92057980ecb0acb0","type":"file","file":"Images/Intro/AboutMe/FragmentDigital/FD_PG_3.jpg","x":-14460,"y":-3425,"width":400,"height":200},
		{"id":"2aaf1939a6aaa83b","type":"file","file":"Images/Intro/AboutMe/RPTU/PHD_14.jpg","x":-14460,"y":-1720,"width":400,"height":137},
		{"id":"f0ff495ab9a98680","type":"file","file":"Images/Intro/AboutMe/FER/M_4.jpg","x":-14460,"y":-830,"width":468,"height":263},
		{"id":"d3bf396bf0feb6fe","type":"file","file":"Images/Intro/AboutMe/RPTU/PHD_2.jpg","x":-14460,"y":-2225,"width":400,"height":248},
		{"id":"25b862fccf91bb7b","type":"file","file":"Images/Intro/AboutMe/RPTU/PHD_12.jpg","x":-14460,"y":-1940,"width":400,"height":199},
		{"id":"d0ddee93f6766996","type":"text","text":"Industry/Tech Art & Procedural","x":-15385,"y":-3394,"width":289,"height":69},
		{"id":"0b7b4fed8e9335d0","type":"text","text":"Procedural modeling is modeling approach where model (geometry, texture, story, terrain, etc.) is described by a set of rules and algorithms applied on certain data (e.g., geometry).\n\nRules are either written in certain programming language (e.g., c++, python, VEX, OSL, GLSL, etc.) or using node based system (visual programming).\n\nResulting model is completely described by a set of rules. Each of rule can be changed completely or by parameters resulting in different version of a model.\n\nMany advantages come out of this approach as we will see. However, it is not a silver bullet!","x":-12623,"y":520,"width":631,"height":332},
		{"id":"b49f16cc02bb0f07","type":"link","url":"https://perso.telecom-paristech.fr/boubek/papers/DAG_Amendment/","x":-12031,"y":-400,"width":1051,"height":796},
		{"id":"ea88091abee1da69","type":"text","text":"Procedural modeling = algorithmical modeling\n* Creating 3D model from parametric rule set, rather than manually\n\t* \"Model\" can be any part of 2D/3D scene: geometry, texture, material, etc.\n\t* \"Parameters\" can by anything from single scalar value to animated geometry with attributes","x":-11920,"y":-2180,"width":631,"height":180},
		{"id":"346db52a3351db37","type":"text","text":"**Authoring step**: creating the algorithm\n> A process or set of rules to be followed in calculations or other problem-solving operations, especially by a computer.","x":-12480,"y":-1871,"width":488,"height":140},
		{"id":"28961332a9600b4b","type":"file","file":"Images/Intro/ProcParadigms/Algorithm.jpg","x":-12479,"y":-1692,"width":487,"height":387},
